-- Opening a module must not re-declare the opaque constants (postulates, abstract definitions)
-- that it re-exports when the module was loaded from its cache. Otherwise copies multiply along
-- the import graph and are stored in the caches of modules rechecked later (in graytt, this made
-- PropTrunc's trunc be declared 51 times when opening Fibration, and some modules take minutes).
--
-- `open` skips a field already bound to the same value (already_bound in src/lang.ml), as decided
-- by V.same_head (src/value.ml), which compares opaque constants by identifier: physical equality
-- does not suffice, since an opaque constant is a fresh value each time the record is evaluated
-- (e.g. from a cache).
--
-- The test suite does not check this automatically: from this directory (d is an ordinary
-- definition, p a postulate, a abstract), with the modules cached (run once after rm -f *.batto),
--
--   batt --debug open-opaque.batt | grep -cE '^DECL +p = '
--
-- should give 1, like for d, and should still do so after editing open-opaque-B.batt and
-- open-opaque-C.batt so that they are rechecked against cached modules.

open import open-opaque-C
open import open-opaque-D
